  "raw": {
    "https://www.avondale.edu.au/job/cultural-support-officer/": {
      "title": "Cultural Support Officer",
      "description": "Cultural Support Officer - Avondale University Current Students Staff Library Alumni News & Events HOME CURRENT STUDENTS STAFF LIBRARY ALUMNI NEWS & EVENTS SHOP DONATE YOUR UNI STUDY RESEARCH YOUR UNI Who We Are Our Purpose History Learning & Teaching Rankings & Achievements Faculty & Schools Academic Integrity Campuses CASTL Schools Engagement Venue & Facility Hire STUDENT LIFE Support Services Accommodation Spiritual Life Service Opportunities Student Associations Sport & Fitness FOLLOW US ONLINE COURSES Nursing Teaching Business Ministry Arts Counselling Lifestyle Medicine Science & Mathematics Postgraduate Courses Higher Degrees by Research Vocational Education Training Short Courses NEW STUDENTS Apply Now Pathways Not sure what to study? Early Entry Fees & costs Scholarships International Students Units Offered Ace Lab RESEARCH AT AVONDALE Researcher Profiles Research Integrity & Ethics Strategy & Performance Research Training & Support RESEARCH CENTRES Christian Education Health, Nursing & Lifestyle Medicine Scripture, Spirituality & Society PUBLICATIONS ACORA Reporting Your Publications TEACH Journal PARTNER ENTITIES EGW Research Centre Adventist Heritage Centre ENQUIRE NOW → Avondale » Cultural Support Officer Cultural Support Officer Cooranbong, NSW Full-time Avondale University is seeking a Cultural Support Officer to join the Deputy Vice Chancellor Academic team on an initial full-time 2-year contract. Contract renewal is conditional on funding approval. Be challenged and imagine with us This exciting role involves working with staff and students to support people of different cultures. What will you do? Some of the main duties will include: Student Support Provide culturally safe support and advice for students on the Lake Macquarie Campus and online students, with a primary but not exclusive focus on students of Aboriginal or Torres Strait Island descent. Assist in the creation of culturally appropriate student resources. Staff Support Provide advice and feedback for staff on all matters relating to cultural awareness and cross-cultural communication. Provide assistance for academic staff seeking culturally appropriate and authentic content and perspectives, especially indigenous, for course development across all fields of study. Liaison and Coordination Assist with building relationships and partnerships to support Avondale in the areas of curriculum development, cultural events, and guest lecturers and speakers. Ensure consistent application of policies, procedures, and service standards in all communications. Compliance and Quality Maintain confidentiality and exercise discretion when handling sensitive information. Maintain accurate records of activities and outcomes. About you To be successful in the Cultural Support Officer role, you will be a dynamic and responsive team player committed to providing guidance and support for Univeristy staff and students that lead to effective and appropriate communivaiton between people of different cultures. Essential criteria A willingness to strongly support the mission, values, and ethos of Avondale. Demonstrated understanding of Aboriginal cultural protocols and cultural safety, with the ability to build and maintain respectful relationships and partnerships with Aboriginal communities and to engage effectively with diverse stakeholders. Strong written and verbal communication skills, with a demonstrated ability to work effectively in cross-cultural contexts. Well-developed organisational skills and the ability to manage competing priorities. Ability to work collaboratively with a wide range of diverse stakeholders and in different cultural contexts. Proficiency in Microsoft Office, willingness and demonstrated ability to learn University systems and procedures. Cooperate with all work health and safety policies and procedures related to the work being undertaken and ensure that their actions or omissions do not impact on the health and safety of others at Avondale.  Promote a safe workplace and identify unsafe practices. Understand and support equal opportunity principles. Desirable criteria Be of Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander descent. Applicant's race is a genuine occupational qualification and is authorised by Section 14 of the Anti-Discrimination Act 1977, NSW. Familiarity with university policies, procedures, or student administration systems. Experience supporting academic staff or course administration functions. Understanding of the student lifecycle and common course-related processes. Please visit www.avondale.edu.au/employment for the job description and details of this position. For further information about the role, please email Avondale University’s People and Culture Manager at jolisa.rabo@avondale.edu.au . Email your application to employment@avondale.edu.au , including: A resume (four-page maximum) A statement addressing the selection criteria Contact details of three referees Please note that we will be conducting interviews as applications come in, so please do not delay in submitting your application. Salary: Avondale Higher Education Worker Level 5 $77,375 - $86,586 per annum, plus superannuation. Applicants must have the right to work in Australia. Avondale is an equal opportunity employer and reserves the right to make a delayed appointment, not appoint, or appoint by invitation. Download Job Description ASK A QUESTION LIVE CHAT CALL Ask a question \" * \" indicates required fields Student type: * Select... Domestic (Australia or New Zealand) International Personal Details Your Name * First Name Family Name/Surname: Mobile Phone Number: * Email Address: * Email Address Confirm Email Address I am.. * Select... a High School Student a Parent/Guardian a Teacher looking at postgraduate study other Current School Year: * Select... Year 12 Year 11 Year 10 Year 9 Other I am interested in: * Select... Arts (Chaplaincy, Communications, Counselling, English, History, Music, Psychology, Visual Art) Business Individual Support Lifestyle Medicine Ministry & Theology Nursing Outdoor Leadership Science Research Degrees Teaching Unsure/Other How did you hear about us? * Select... At School Bus Advertisement Career Expos Church/Church Big Camps Good Universities Guide Google Printed material (course guide, leaflet, brochure) Radio Record Magazine Social Media (Facebook, Instagram, LinkedIN) UAC website Word of Mouth (friends, family, teachers) Other Your message: * By submitting this form, you consent to Avondale University collecting your information for the purpose of responding to your enquiry and providing relevant information about the University. Your information will remain confidential and will not be shared with third parties. Submit About Us Who We Are History Our Purpose Campuses Research Jobs Policies Online Store Terms of Use Copyright Study Courses International Students Student Profile Fees and Costs Scholarships Getting Started Units Offered & Fees Student Employment Pathways Into University Work Integrated Learning Courses Nursing Teaching Business Ministry Arts Counselling Lifestyle Medicine Science & Mathematics VET & Short Courses Postgraduate Student Life Avondale Student Life Accommodation Campuses Food on Campus Student Support Services Spiritual Life Sport and Fitness Student Associations Service Opportunities Research TEACH Journal Higher Degrees by Research ACORA Strategy & Performance Research Integrity & Ethics Research Training & Support Christian Education Research Centre Lifestyle Medicine and Health Research Centre Scripture, Spirituality and Society Research Centre Avondale Academic Press News Research News Avondale Business School Avondale Conservatorium Avondale Alumni Events Course Enquiries 582 Freemans Drive, Cooranbong NSW 2265 Australia Phone: +61 2 4980 2377 Email: study@avondale.edu.au Lake Macquarie Campus - Main Campus 582 Freemans Drive, Cooranbong NSW 2265 Australia Phone: +61 2 4980 2222 Email: reception@avondale.edu.au Sydney Campus 185 Fox Valley Road, Wahroonga NSW 2076 Australia Phone: +61 2 9480 3630 Email: campus.manager@avondale.edu.au Visit our Facebook Visit our Instagram Visit our LinkedIn Visit our YouTube channel Avondale University acknowledges our Sovereign God as Creator and Provider of all things. We respectfully acknowledge the Awabakal and Darramuragal people as the traditional custodians of the lands on which we live, work, study and worship across our Lake Macquarie and Sydney campuses. We pay our respects to Elders past, present and emerging, and extend that respect to all First Nations People. Avondale University is a member of the worldwide Seventh-day Adventist system of universities and colleges. CRICOS Provider No.: 02731D.    RTO: 91191.   TEQSA: PRV12015.   ABN: 53 108 186 401. © Avondale University Ltd 2026 Contact Copyright Privacy search close chevron-right chevron-down facebook-square bars instagram linkedin facebook pinterest youtube rss twitter instagram facebook-blank rss-blank linkedin-blank pinterest youtube twitter instagram Notifications"
