    "https://www.avondale.edu.au/job/residential-life-co-ordinator-womens-residence/": {
      "title": "Residential Life Co-Ordinator (women's residence)",
      "description": "Residential Life Co-Ordinator (women's residence) - Avondale University Current Students Staff Library Alumni News & Events HOME CURRENT STUDENTS STAFF LIBRARY ALUMNI NEWS & EVENTS SHOP DONATE YOUR UNI STUDY RESEARCH YOUR UNI Who We Are Our Purpose History Learning & Teaching Rankings & Achievements Faculty & Schools Academic Integrity Campuses CASTL Schools Engagement Venue & Facility Hire STUDENT LIFE Support Services Accommodation Spiritual Life Service Opportunities Student Associations Sport & Fitness FOLLOW US ONLINE COURSES Nursing Teaching Business Ministry Arts Counselling Lifestyle Medicine Science & Mathematics Postgraduate Courses Higher Degrees by Research Vocational Education Training Short Courses NEW STUDENTS Apply Now Pathways Not sure what to study? Early Entry Fees & costs Scholarships International Students Units Offered Ace Lab RESEARCH AT AVONDALE Researcher Profiles Research Integrity & Ethics Strategy & Performance Research Training & Support RESEARCH CENTRES Christian Education Health, Nursing & Lifestyle Medicine Scripture, Spirituality & Society PUBLICATIONS ACORA Reporting Your Publications TEACH Journal PARTNER ENTITIES EGW Research Centre Adventist Heritage Centre ENQUIRE NOW → Avondale » Residential Life Co-Ordinator (women's residence) Residential Life Co-Ordinator (women's residence) Lake Macquarie Campus, NSW Part-time (32 hrs per week) Avondale University is seeking applications for a part-time Residential Life Co-Ordinator (women’s residence) for 32 hours per week. Be part of the transformation. This important role will have you at the front lines of the Avondale student experience. The Residential Life Co-ordinator facilitates the co-ordination of the residences as a community and is dedicated to delivering a residential life education program designed to create an environment in which students are supported and encouraged to participate in activities and events that support faith-development, foster wellbeing, academic success and social engagement. What will you do? Some of the main duties will include (see full job description for more details): Create and support an environment of respect, inclusivity, collegiality, and personal responsibility through role modelling, and educating others to expected community standards. Prioritise and respond to residents’ needs, tolerate interruptions of personal time and space and maintain a high profile and active presence within the residential communities, developing rapport with residents. Contribute to benchmarking of educational programs and services against Australian and international accommodation providers, adopting a continuous improvement approach towards duties and responsibilities. Respond to incidents or concerns regarding resident behaviour or wellbeing, working closely with the Chief Students and Engagement Officer, university support services and student leadership teams to ensure the wellbeing of the residential community. Primary accountability for facilitating the academic support for residential students as needed. Consultative responsibility for spiritual support programs for residential students. Shared accountability for facilitating and coordinating the implementation of various well-being initiatives, reporting and conducting check-ins for student well-being. Participate in and provide input and support for the wider needs of Student Life Services, such as; Orientation programs Student leadership training programs Student wellbeing weeks Graduation activities and services About you To be successful in the Residential Life Co-ordinator role, you will have previous experience in a similar role, be highly productive, empathetic, and enthusiastic. You will poses strong organisational skills with event management experience and great communication skills with the capacity to collaborate and contribute to the development of a positive and co-operative team environment. Essential criteria A baptised and practicing member of the Seventh-day Adventist Church. Supportive and committed to promoting the Adventist mission, ethos and values of Avondale by influence and example. Be willing to participate actively in the spiritual, cultural and recreational life of the campus Demonstrated experience in dealing effectively and empathically with young adults, building strong social interaction with others of different socio-economic and cultural backgrounds, and be accepting of diversity and individual differences Demonstrated ability and capacity to contribute to the development of a positive and co-operative team environment Sound organisational and time management skills including the ability to plan, implement and co-ordinate the delivery of educational programs Effective interpersonal skills and written and verbal communication skills that can be adapted for various audiences Skills and knowledge in various common sports and equipment requirements Advanced level of computer literacy with excellent skills in Microsoft Office applications Capacity to identify, assess, prioritise and control the risks to the health and safety of staff, residents and visitors and to the environment arising from residential and sporting activities Support the mission, values, and ethos of Avondale Desirable criteria Current manual C Class Driver’s Licence An Education, Social Work, Youth Work, Psychology, Counselling or Chaplaincy undergraduate or post graduate degree Why work at Avondale? Half day Friday’s Heavily discounted further study options Discounted school fees for attendance at Adventist schools Free access to onsite ovals, tennis courts, squash courts and Auditorium on Lake Macquarie campus during opening hours Free access to Avondale Libraries Café on Lake Macquarie Campus Values driven organisation Please visit www.avondale.edu.au/employment for the full job description and details of this position. For further information about the role, please email Avondale University’s People and Culture Manager at jolisa.rabo@avondale.edu.au . Email your application to employment@avondale.edu.au , including: A resume (four-page maximum) A statement addressing the selection criteria Contact details of three referees Salary: Avondale Higher Education Worker Level 7 $51.31 - $57.87 per hour, plus superannuation. Please note that we will be conducting interviews as applications come in, so please do not delay in submitting your application. Applications close on 13 November 2026 Applicants must have the right to work in Australia. Avondale is an equal opportunity employer and reserves the right to make a delayed appointment, not appoint, or appoint by invitation. Download Job Description ASK A QUESTION LIVE CHAT CALL Ask a question \" * \" indicates required fields Student type: * Select... Domestic (Australia or New Zealand) International Personal Details Your Name * First Name Family Name/Surname: Mobile Phone Number: * Email Address: * Email Address Confirm Email Address I am.. * Select... a High School Student a Parent/Guardian a Teacher looking at postgraduate study other Current School Year: * Select... Year 12 Year 11 Year 10 Year 9 Other I am interested in: * Select... Arts (Chaplaincy, Communications, Counselling, English, History, Music, Psychology, Visual Art) Business Individual Support Lifestyle Medicine Ministry & Theology Nursing Outdoor Leadership Science Research Degrees Teaching Unsure/Other How did you hear about us? * Select... At School Bus Advertisement Career Expos Church/Church Big Camps Good Universities Guide Google Printed material (course guide, leaflet, brochure) Radio Record Magazine Social Media (Facebook, Instagram, LinkedIN) UAC website Word of Mouth (friends, family, teachers) Other Your message: * By submitting this form, you consent to Avondale University collecting your information for the purpose of responding to your enquiry and providing relevant information about the University. Your information will remain confidential and will not be shared with third parties. Submit About Us Who We Are History Our Purpose Campuses Research Jobs Policies Online Store Terms of Use Copyright Study Courses International Students Student Profile Fees and Costs Scholarships Getting Started Units Offered & Fees Student Employment Pathways Into University Work Integrated Learning Courses Nursing Teaching Business Ministry Arts Counselling Lifestyle Medicine Science & Mathematics VET & Short Courses Postgraduate Student Life Avondale Student Life Accommodation Campuses Food on Campus Student Support Services Spiritual Life Sport and Fitness Student Associations Service Opportunities Research TEACH Journal Higher Degrees by Research ACORA Strategy & Performance Research Integrity & Ethics Research Training & Support Christian Education Research Centre Lifestyle Medicine and Health Research Centre Scripture, Spirituality and Society Research Centre Avondale Academic Press News Research News Avondale Business School Avondale Conservatorium Avondale Alumni Events Course Enquiries 582 Freemans Drive, Cooranbong NSW 2265 Australia Phone: +61 2 4980 2377 Email: study@avondale.edu.au Lake Macquarie Campus - Main Campus 582 Freemans Drive, Cooranbong NSW 2265 Australia Phone: +61 2 4980 2222 Email: reception@avondale.edu.au Sydney Campus 185 Fox Valley Road, Wahroonga NSW 2076 Australia Phone: +61 2 9480 3630 Email: campus.manager@avondale.edu.au Visit our Facebook Visit our Instagram Visit our LinkedIn Visit our YouTube channel Avondale University acknowledges our Sovereign God as Creator and Provider of all things. We respectfully acknowledge the Awabakal and Darramuragal people as the traditional custodians of the lands on which we live, work, study and worship across our Lake Macquarie and Sydney campuses. We pay our respects to Elders past, present and emerging, and extend that respect to all First Nations People. Avondale University is a member of the worldwide Seventh-day Adventist system of universities an