    "https://www.avondale.edu.au/job/student-administration-services-officer/": {
      "title": "Student Administration Services Officer",
      "description": "Student Administration Services Officer - Avondale University Current Students Staff Library Alumni News & Events HOME CURRENT STUDENTS STAFF LIBRARY ALUMNI NEWS & EVENTS SHOP DONATE YOUR UNI STUDY RESEARCH YOUR UNI Who We Are Our Purpose History Learning & Teaching Rankings & Achievements Faculty & Schools Academic Integrity Campuses CASTL Schools Engagement Venue & Facility Hire STUDENT LIFE Support Services Accommodation Spiritual Life Service Opportunities Student Associations Sport & Fitness FOLLOW US ONLINE COURSES Nursing Teaching Business Ministry Arts Counselling Lifestyle Medicine Science & Mathematics Postgraduate Courses Higher Degrees by Research Vocational Education Training Short Courses NEW STUDENTS Apply Now Pathways Not sure what to study? Early Entry Fees & costs Scholarships International Students Units Offered Ace Lab RESEARCH AT AVONDALE Researcher Profiles Research Integrity & Ethics Strategy & Performance Research Training & Support RESEARCH CENTRES Christian Education Health, Nursing & Lifestyle Medicine Scripture, Spirituality & Society PUBLICATIONS ACORA Reporting Your Publications TEACH Journal PARTNER ENTITIES EGW Research Centre Adventist Heritage Centre ENQUIRE NOW → Avondale » Student Administration Services Officer Student Administration Services Officer Lake Macquarie Campus, NSW Full-time, 6 month fixed-term contract (parental leave relief) Avondale University is seeking a Student Administration Services (SAS) Officer to join the SAS team on a full-time 6 month fixed-term contract (parental leave relief) until May 2027. Be challenged and imagine with us This exciting role will have you at the front lines of the Avondale student journey, from initial enquiry to admission right through to graduation. You will be responsible for providing courteous, efficient and professional customer service to staff, students and other relevant stakeholders. What will you do? Some of the main duties will include: Action the administrative processes with regard to student academic management. Process requests for transcripts, unit outlines, statements of attainment and testamurs. Processing and distribution of regular reports on information including but not limited to, student progression, intermissions and discontinuations, probation, course transfers and student demographics. Maintain student records in Avondale’s Student Management System and relevant filing systems. Maintain an operational knowledge of government legislation, policies and standards as it relates to student management, international students and progression. Process tasks associated with the organisation and administration of the Exam Centre. Process tasks associated with the organisation and production of academic aspects associated with Graduation. Provide expert customer service to students and staff in relation to their enquiries. Liaise with Course Convenors where relevant. Prepare relevant correspondence for students as required. About you To be successful in the Student Administration Services Officer role, you will be a dynamic and responsive team player committed to positively impacting students and the wider Avondale community. You will thrive under pressure and possess a can-do attitude. Essential criteria Completion of a minimum qualification at a certificate IV level with subsequent relevant work experience; or extensive relevant experience and specialist expertise; or an equivalent combination of relevant experience and/or education/training; Demonstrated interpersonal skills and communications, including a professional and confident telephone manner and effective liaison skills; High level of computer literacy, including ability to use databases, Microsoft Office suite of programs (i.e. Word, Excel, Outlook,  etc.), and internet; or demonstrated ability to gain and apply such knowledge within a short timeframe; Demonstrated organisational skills, especially in a high-volume outcome-based service environment, including ability to monitor work processes and meet deadlines with capacity to work extended hours during peak periods; Demonstrated experience of effective teamwork and ability to work under minimal direct supervision; Demonstrated commitment to customer service standards and ability to liaise effectively staff and management as well as varying personalities and people situations; A high level of accuracy and attention to detail Ability to maintain confidentiality when dealing with personal information and information of a sensitive nature; Demonstrated ability to cooperate with work health and safety policies and procedures ensuring actions or omissions do not impact on the health and safety of others; Supportive of the mission, values, and ethos of Avondale. Desirable criteria An undergraduate degree; Experience in administration, preferably within the Higher Education and/or VET sector/s; Experience using student administration software/databases (Callista, Moodle) would be highly desirable. Please visit www.avondale.edu.au/employment for the job description and details of this position. For further information about the role, please email Avondale University’s People and Culture Manager at jolisa.rabo@avondale.edu.au . Email your application to employment@avondale.edu.au , including: A resume (four-page maximum) A statement addressing the selection criteria Contact details of three referees Applications close on 13 November 2026 Please note that we will be conducting interviews as applications come in, so please do not delay in submitting your application. Salary: Avondale Higher Education Worker Level 4 $73,619 - $77,340 per annum, plus superannuation. Applicants must have the right to work in Australia. Avondale is an equal opportunity employer and reserves the right to make a delayed appointment, not appoint, or appoint by invitation. Download Job Description ASK A QUESTION LIVE CHAT CALL Ask a question \" * \" indicates required fields Student type: *