      "title": "Jobs - Avondale University",
      "description": "Jobs - Avondale University Current Students Staff Library Alumni News & Events HOME CURRENT STUDENTS STAFF LIBRARY ALUMNI NEWS & EVENTS SHOP DONATE YOUR UNI STUDY RESEARCH YOUR UNI Who We Are Our Purpose History Learning & Teaching Rankings & Achievements Faculty & Schools Academic Integrity Campuses CASTL Schools Engagement Venue & Facility Hire STUDENT LIFE Support Services Accommodation Spiritual Life Service Opportunities Student Associations Sport & Fitness FOLLOW US ONLINE COURSES Nursing Teaching Business Ministry Arts Counselling Lifestyle Medicine Science & Mathematics Postgraduate Courses Higher Degrees by Research Vocational Education Training Short Courses NEW STUDENTS Apply Now Pathways Not sure what to study? Early Entry Fees & costs Scholarships International Students Units Offered Ace Lab RESEARCH AT AVONDALE Researcher Profiles Research Integrity & Ethics Strategy & Performance Research Training & Support RESEARCH CENTRES Christian Education Health, Nursing & Lifestyle Medicine Scripture, Spirituality & Society PUBLICATIONS ACORA Reporting Your Publications TEACH Journal PARTNER ENTITIES EGW Research Centre Adventist Heritage Centre ENQUIRE NOW → Jobs Avondale » Jobs Why Avondale? We believe in a Christ-centred education with a greater vision of world needs. Working with us means your role has a ripple effect on not just our community but the world at large. Join our team of dedicated academic and professional staff to start making a difference. Our Values We are a value focused community. Our values of Excellence, Spirituality, Wellbeing, Integrity and Service are at the centre of everything we do. Our Culture We strive for excellence in higher education, as demonstrated in our number one university ranking. Staff Benefits We offer staff benefits as a way to thank you for your contribution. Adventist school subsidies, generous leave entitlements, discounted units of study, and additional super based on years of service are some of the many benefits for our staff. Avondale is committed to creating a safe space for all staff, students and community members. As part of the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-Based Violence 2025, Avondale will consider gender-based violence risk factors as part of the recruitment process. As part of the recruitment process, candidates who progress to the interview stage will need to complete and return the University’s Gender-based Violence Declaration Form. Other forms may include a Working with Children Check, Police Check or any other pre-employment checks appropriate to the role. Avondale University Positions Cultural Support Officer Residential Life Co-Ordinator (women's residence) Student Administration Services Officer 7@Avondale Positions Contact People and Culture at Avondale University. Visit Adventist Employment for positions vacant at other entities of the Seventh-day Adventist Church in the South Pacific . Adventist Employment Student Employment Avondale University employs students on a casual basis for help in various roles. Students seeking casual employment should complete the Student Worker Application . Employment will require the provision of Avondale’s Student Engagement Form, bank account details and a taxation declaration. Students can obtain these forms from each department once employment is offered. Student Worker Application ASK A QUESTION LIVE CHAT CALL Ask a question \" * \" indicates required fields Student type: * Select... Domestic (Australia or New Zealand) International Personal Details Your Name * First Name Family Name/Surname: Mobile Phone Number: * Email Address: * Email Address Confirm Email Address I am.. * Select... a High School Student a Parent/Guardian a Teacher looking at postgraduate study other Current School Year: * Select... Year 12 Year 11 Year 10 Year 9 Other I am interested in: * Select... Arts (Chaplaincy, Communications, Counselling, English, History, Music, Psychology, Visual A